.TH yabai 1  "yabai 7.1.25" "Yabai Manual"
.SH NAME
yabai \- Tiling window manager for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fByabai\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tiling window manager for macOS.
.PP
Without a command, runs the window manager itself; the launchd service runs it that way. Every other command is sent to the running window manager, except `service` and `scripting\-addition`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Config file the window manager runs at start\-up [default: the first yabairc found]

Without this option, the first of $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yabai/yabairc, ~/.config/yabai/yabairc and ~/.yabairc that exists. An executable file runs as `sh \-c FILE`, any other as `sh FILE`.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print debug information to stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "yabai service"
.PP
Manage the launchd service (~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.asmvik.yabai.plist)
.SS "yabai service install"
.PP
Write the launchd service file
.SS "yabai service uninstall"
.PP
Remove the launchd service file
.SS "yabai service start"
.PP
Install the service file if it is missing, then enable, load and start the service
.SS "yabai service restart"
.PP
Restart the running service
.SS "yabai service stop"
.PP
Stop the running service
.SS "yabai scripting-addition"
.PP
Load or uninstall the Dock scripting addition (System Integrity Protection must be partially disabled)
.SS "yabai scripting-addition load"
.PP
Install the scripting addition if it is missing or outdated, then load it into the Dock (run as root)
.SS "yabai scripting-addition uninstall"
.PP
Remove the scripting addition (run as root)
.SS "yabai config"
.PP
Change or print the settings of the window manager
.SS "yabai config set"
.PP
\fByabai config set\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-space\fR] [\fB\-\-layout\fR] [\fB\-\-split\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-top\-padding\fR] [\fB\-\-bottom\-padding\fR] [\fB\-\-left\-padding\fR] [\fB\-\-right\-padding\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-gap\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-balance\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-reload\-config\-file\-on\-change\fR] [\fB\-\-external\-bar\fR] [\fB\-\-menubar\-opacity\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\-follows\-focus\fR] [\fB\-\-focus\-follows\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-display\-arrangement\-order\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-origin\-display\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-placement\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-insertion\-point\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-zoom\-persist\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-window\-focus\-animation\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-shadow\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-opacity\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-opacity\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-active\-window\-opacity\fR] [\fB\-\-normal\-window\-opacity\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-animation\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-animation\-easing\fR] [\fB\-\-insert\-feedback\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-background\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-active\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-inactive\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-active\-text\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-inactive\-text\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-font\-family\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-font\-style\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-header\-font\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-split\-ratio\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\-modifier\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\-action1\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\-action2\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\-drop\-action\fR] 
.PP
Change settings; every value is checked before any setting changes
.PP
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-space\fR \fI<SPACE_SEL>\fR
Give one space its own values instead of changing the global ones, which the space then ignores
.TP
\fB\-\-layout\fR \fI<LAYOUT>\fR
Tile windows as a binary tree (bsp), pile them up (stack) or leave them be (float)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bsp
.IP \(bu 2
stack
.IP \(bu 2
float
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-split\-type\fR \fI<SPLIT_TYPE>\fR
Split along the y\-axis (vertical), the x\-axis (horizontal) or the longer side (auto)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
vertical
.IP \(bu 2
horizontal
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-top\-padding\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Padding at the top of the space, in points
.TP
\fB\-\-bottom\-padding\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Padding at the bottom of the space, in points
.TP
\fB\-\-left\-padding\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Padding at the left of the space, in points
.TP
\fB\-\-right\-padding\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Padding at the right of the space, in points
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-gap\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Gap between two tiled windows, in points
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-balance\fR \fI<AUTO_BALANCE>\fR
Balance the tree after every change, along both axes, one axis or none
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
x\-axis
.IP \(bu 2
y\-axis
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\-output\fR \fI<DEBUG_OUTPUT>\fR
Print debug information to stdout
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-reload\-config\-file\-on\-change\fR \fI<RELOAD_CONFIG_FILE_ON_CHANGE>\fR
Run the config file again whenever it changes; label rules and signals so that a reload replaces them instead of adding them again
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-external\-bar\fR \fI<MODE:TOP:BOTTOM>\fR
Keep room for a status bar on the main display, on every display, or nowhere
.TP
\fB\-\-menubar\-opacity\fR \fI<OPACITY>\fR
Opacity of the menu bar, from 0 to 1; at 0 it no longer takes clicks
.TP
\fB\-\-mouse\-follows\-focus\fR \fI<MOUSE_FOLLOWS_FOCUS>\fR
Put the cursor at the centre of a window yabai focuses
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-focus\-follows\-mouse\fR \fI<FOCUS_FOLLOWS_MOUSE>\fR
Focus the window under the cursor, raising it (autoraise) or not (autofocus)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
autofocus
.IP \(bu 2
autoraise
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-display\-arrangement\-order\fR \fI<DISPLAY_ARRANGEMENT_ORDER>\fR
Order display indexes as macOS does, by x first (horizontal) or by y first (vertical)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
default
.IP \(bu 2
horizontal
.IP \(bu 2
vertical
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-origin\-display\fR \fI<WINDOW_ORIGIN_DISPLAY>\fR
Manage a new window on the display it opened on, the focused display, or the one under the cursor
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
default
.IP \(bu 2
focused
.IP \(bu 2
cursor
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-placement\fR \fI<WINDOW_PLACEMENT>\fR
Which child a new window becomes when it splits a window
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
second\-child
.IP \(bu 2
first\-child
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-insertion\-point\fR \fI<WINDOW_INSERTION_POINT>\fR
Which window a new window splits
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
focused
.IP \(bu 2
first
.IP \(bu 2
last
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-zoom\-persist\fR \fI<WINDOW_ZOOM_PERSIST>\fR
Keep windows zoomed through layout changes
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-window\-focus\-animation\fR \fI<SKIP_WINDOW_FOCUS_ANIMATION>\fR
Skip the space animation when a window on another space gets focus; only without the scripting addition, which does it better
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-shadow\fR \fI<WINDOW_SHADOW>\fR
Draw window shadows, none, or only on floating windows (needs the scripting addition)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
float
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-opacity\fR \fI<WINDOW_OPACITY>\fR
Give focused and unfocused windows their own opacity (needs the scripting addition)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-opacity\-duration\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Seconds an opacity change takes
.TP
\fB\-\-active\-window\-opacity\fR \fI<OPACITY>\fR
Opacity of the focused window, above 0 up to 1
.TP
\fB\-\-normal\-window\-opacity\fR \fI<OPACITY>\fR
Opacity of unfocused windows, above 0 up to 1
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-animation\-duration\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Seconds a window takes to move into place; above 0 needs the scripting addition and Screen Recording
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-animation\-easing\fR \fI<WINDOW_ANIMATION_EASING>\fR
Easing curve of window animations (see https://easings.net)
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-sine
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-sine
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-sine
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-quad
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-quad
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-quad
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-cubic
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-cubic
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-cubic
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-quart
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-quart
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-quart
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-quint
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-quint
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-quint
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-expo
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-expo
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-expo
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-circ
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-out\-circ
.IP \(bu 2
ease\-in\-out\-circ
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-insert\-feedback\-color\fR \fI<0xAARRGGBB>\fR
Colour of the insertion preview, 0xAARRGGBB other than 0; until it is set, the accent colour
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-height\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Height of the tab header of a window group, in points; 0 draws none
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-background\-color\fR \fI<0xAARRGGBB>\fR
Colour of the bar behind the tabs of a group; 0x00000000 draws none
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-active\-color\fR \fI<0xAARRGGBB>\fR
Colour of the tab of the window in front of its group
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-inactive\-color\fR \fI<0xAARRGGBB>\fR
Colour of the tabs of the other windows of a group
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-active\-text\-color\fR \fI<0xAARRGGBB>\fR
Colour of the title in the tab of the window in front of its group
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-inactive\-text\-color\fR \fI<0xAARRGGBB>\fR
Colour of the titles in the tabs of the other windows of a group
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-font\-family\fR \fI<FAMILY>\fR
Font family of the tab titles, as Font Book lists it
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-font\-style\fR \fI<STYLE>\fR
Font style of the tab titles, such as Bold; empty for the regular style
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-header\-font\-size\fR \fI<POINTS>\fR
Size of the tab titles, in points
.TP
\fB\-\-split\-ratio\fR \fI<RATIO>\fR
Share of the area a split gives its first child, from 0.1 to 0.9
.TP
\fB\-\-mouse\-modifier\fR \fI<MOUSE_MODIFIER>\fR
Key held to move or resize windows with the mouse
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
cmd
.IP \(bu 2
alt
.IP \(bu 2
shift
.IP \(bu 2
ctrl
.IP \(bu 2
fn
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mouse\-action1\fR \fI<MOUSE_ACTION1>\fR
What the left button does while the modifier is held
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
move
.IP \(bu 2
resize
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mouse\-action2\fR \fI<MOUSE_ACTION2>\fR
What the right button does while the modifier is held
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
move
.IP \(bu 2
resize
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mouse\-drop\-action\fR \fI<MOUSE_DROP_ACTION>\fR
What dropping a tiled window on the centre of another does
.br
.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
swap
.IP \(bu 2
stack
.RE
