.SS "yabai rule add"
.PP
\fByabai rule add\fR [\fB\-\-one\-shot\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-\-app\fR] [\fB\-\-app\-not\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-title\-not\fR] [\fB\-\-role\fR] [\fB\-\-role\-not\fR] [\fB\-\-subrole\fR] [\fB\-\-subrole\-not\fR] [\fB\-\-display\fR] [\fB\-\-space\fR] [\fB\-\-follow\fR] [\fB\-\-manage\fR] [\fB\-\-sticky\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\-follows\-focus\fR] [\fB\-\-sub\-layer\fR] [\fB\-\-opacity\fR] [\fB\-\-native\-fullscreen\fR] [\fB\-\-grid\fR] [\fB\-\-scratchpad\fR] 
.PP
Add a rule for the windows that open from now on
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-one\-shot\fR
Remove the rule once it has applied to one window
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
A later rule with the same label replaces this one
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR \fI<REGEX>\fR
Match windows whose application name matches REGEX
.TP
\fB\-\-app\-not\fR \fI<REGEX>\fR
Match windows whose application name does not match REGEX
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<REGEX>\fR
